ory_count":4},{"business_id":"_Bi9kN_eR75G1eqIl7S3pA","name":"The Bulldog","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife, Pubs, Restaurants","shared_category_count":4},{"business_id":"kdqoDMuvyNedsouc1i33vQ","name":"Araña Taqueria y Cantina","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":3},{"business_id":"_C7QiQQc47AOEv4PE3Kong","name":"Commander's Palace","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":3},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"TMBbCDQG6bENJoQSST0XiA","name":"Brigtsen's Restaurant","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"mhrW9O0O5hXGXGnEYBVoag","name":"Jacques-Imo's Cafe","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"8KnMSrMuTI2AtHZ2LOI8OQ","name":"Maurepas Foods","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"-e7vSLH84kk7mzHsesL0Qg","review_id":"AEiIxf6wTk0VSiyfz1778w","date":"2019-04-22T22:09:40","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9538332223892212,"text_excerpt":"This will probably be the shortest review I have done in awhile. My partner and I made a friend out here on our first night and he took us to so many places! Pirates alley Cafe was one of our stops. The drink of choice: real absinthe. From my understand this is the only place licensed to do real wormwood absinthe and it was worth it. The interior is pretty cool but what you would think a pirate bar would be. Divey and local vibe which was nice. Unfortunately we didn't stay long enough to enjoy the bar. Down the hatch and back to the streets for more fun. If you come out to new Orleans come by and check them out. Super fun."},{"business_id":"-e7vSLH84kk7mzHsesL0Qg","review_id":"97vtSaLJJIQPgBrTlCkyMg","date":"2009-04-12T04:01:26","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9423558712005615,"text_excerpt":"When I asked a local about this place, I got an eye roll. That didn't stop us from checking it out though. Pirates? Come on! Ya gotta stop by. The bartender was super friendly, the drinks were reasonably priced, and the absinthe prep was pretty cool. I've only had home-brewed absinthe before (and boy did it kick my butt!) but it tasted nothing like this. This absinthe was like liquid black licorice, and rather refreshing. I'm not a fan of black licorice, so I wouldnt order it again, here or elsewhere, but I think my sis has found her new favorite drink! There is a cute seating area outside, which I fully reccommend if you are a people watcher. If I'm ever in New Orleans again, I'd go back."},{"business_id":"-e7vSLH84kk7mzHsesL0Qg","review_id":"bmawcI5mUKtA2wlzx0FNSQ","date":"2019-01-10T04:20:43","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9351352453231812,"text_excerpt":"Wife and I came down here for our first time absinthe experience. The bartenders dress up as pirates and the inside is dark and cozy aka small! We ordered our drinks and the show begins. Not really a show but more of an experience. My wife and I were not big fans of the drink itself but it's a must. It taste like rubbing alcohol, mixed with water, and a splash of licorice for taste and scent. It took us about 50 minutes to finish our cup. Definitely a different buzz, but literally got just a light buzz. My favorite part was the outdoor patio. Great place to lounge and people watch since a bunch of tours come by. I didn't like the fact that it is cash only, and also wish they had some type..."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"-e7vSLH84kk7mzHsesL0Qg","photo_id":"0iTmBxUW5C7IMjA0ELg-bQ","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/0iTmBxUW5C7IMjA0ELg-bQ.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.9164972901344299},{"business_id"